%S A401408 0,1,2,3,4,3,4,5,6,7,6,7,8,7,8,7,8,7,8,9,8,9,10,11,12,13,12,13,14,13,
%T A401408 12,13,14,15,14,13,14,13,14,13,12,11,12,13,14,13,14,15,16,17,18,17,16,
%U A401408 15,16,15,16,17,16,17,16,15,16,17,18,19,20,21,20,21,20,21
%N A401408 Partial sums of A209661.
%C A401408 Denoted as {L(n;4,1)} in the Humphries, Shekatkar, and Wong (2019) article.
%C A401408 a(n) > 0 for 1 < n <= 10^11 (Humphries, Shekatkar, and Wong, "Note on computations"), confirmed by an exact calculation in Gallego 2026, Appendix K.3; the minimum of a(n)/sqrt(n) for 17 <= n <= 10^11 is 7/sqrt(17) = 1.6977..., occurring at n = 17.
%C A401408 Assuming GRH, LI, and the bound (4.10) from Humphries, Shekatkar, and Wong, the argument from their Theorem 4.5, adapted to this sequence in Gallego 2026 (Appendix K), yields a logarithmic mean for a(n)/sqrt(n) equal to (1 + 2^(-1/2))/L(1/2, chi_{-4}) = 2.5567...; this value already appears numerically in Shekatkar and Wong (arXiv v1, Remark 3.10).
%C A401408 It is not known (unconditionally) whether a(n) < 0 for any n.
%H A401408 Leandro Hector Gallego and Jianing Song, <a href="/A401408/b401408.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A401408 Leandro Hector Gallego, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23597138">Explicit sign changes in comparative prime number theory: computer-assisted proofs with checkable certificates</a>, preprint, Zenodo, 2026 (version 1.2). See Appendix K.
%H A401408 Leandro Hector Gallego, <a href="/A401408/a401408_1.jpg">Graph of a(n)/sqrt(n) for n = 10^2..10^11 (exact values at 19322 points: all n up to 999, then about 2300 per decade; logarithmic x-axis)</a>
%H A401408 Peter Humphries, Snehal M. Shekatkar, and Tian An Wong, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5802/jtnb.1066">Biases in prime factorizations and Liouville functions for arithmetic progressions</a>, J. Théor. Nombres Bordeaux 31 (2019), 1-25.
%H A401408 Vaclav Kotesovec, <a href="/A401408/a401408.jpg">Graph - the asymptotic mean (10^7 terms)</a>
%H A401408 Snehal M. Shekatkar and Tian An Wong, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.07979v1">Unexpected biases in prime factorizations and Liouville functions for arithmetic progressions</a>, arXiv:1704.07979v1 [math.NT], 2017.
%F A401408 a(n) = Sum_{k=0..floor(log_2(n))} A401365(floor(n/2^k)) for n >= 1.
%F A401408 a(n) - a(floor(n/2)) = A401365(n).
%F A401408 Dirichlet g.f. of a(n) - a(n-1) (= A209661): (1 + 2^(-s))*zeta(2s)/L(s,chi_{-4}), where chi_{-4} = A101455.
%F A401408 Conjecture: Average value of a(n)/sqrt(n) = (2 + sqrt(2)) / (zeta(1/2, 1/4) - zeta(1/2, 3/4)) = 2.556730002764986782866689... - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Oct 24 2026
%t A401408 f[p_, e_] := If[Mod[p, 4] == 1, (-1)^e, 1]; s[n_] := Times @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; s[0] = 0; s[1] = 1; Accumulate[Array[s, 72, 0]] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 24 2026 *)
%o A401408 (PARI) a(n) = sum(k=1, n, (-1)^(bigomega(k)-valuation(k, 2))*kronecker(-1, k))
%Y A401408 Cf. A209661, A002819, A401365.
%Y A401408 Cf. A068639 ({L(n;2,0)}), -A318682 ({L(n;2,1)}), A062756 ({L(n;3,2)}), this sequence ({L(n;4,1)}), A005811 ({L(n;4,3)}), A401409 ({L(n;4,2,3)}).
